# Local Engineering Rules

## Language Tool Table (Lua 5.4)
- The language table in engineering.prompt does not cover Lua; use this table instead.
- Mutation: `mutate4lua`; CRAP: `crap4lua`; DRY: `dry4lua`; dependency boundaries: `arch-view`. All ship in this repo and run via `lua tools/cli.lua <mutate|crap|dry|arch-view>`; no separate install step is required.
- APS tools (`gherkin-parser`, `ir-dry-checker`, `gherkin-mutator`) are served by the pinned Lua rock
  `acceptance4lua` (`tools/tools.lock`), not by the Babashka/Go builds named in engineering.prompt:
  those cannot read this repo's `# language: zh-CN` features (they fail with
  `missing feature declaration`), so engineering.prompt's "does not work in the current project
  environment" fallback applies here.
- Supply shape: `<swarm-root>/.swarmforge/bin/{gherkin-parser,ir-dry-checker,gherkin-mutator}` are
  project-provisioned bash-to-Lua forwarders onto `tools/packages/acceptance/cli/parser.lua`,
  `tools/packages/acceptance/cli/ir_dry.lua` and `tools/packages/acceptance_mutate/mutator.lua`;
  each entrypoint re-installs its own rock through `bootstrap.ensure_tool`. `<swarm-root>` is the
  directory holding `.swarmforge/roles.tsv` - for an agent worktree that is the `git --git-common-dir`
  parent, i.e. one shared bin/ for all worktrees, the same root `swarm_tool.sh` probes; a worktree's
  own `.swarmforge/` holds only handoff/notify state and never serves these tools. The launcher puts
  that `bin/` first on PATH, so those three files are what "available at next startup" means.
- This article overrides `engineering.prompt` wherever the two meet on this project's tool
  surface - including that article's Tool Startup clause "If it is missing, run exactly
  `swarm_tool.sh ensure <tool>`", which the launcher also repeats in every pane's `## Tool Startup`
  section. Obeying it here is not hypothetical: it replaced the provisioned Lua forwarders with
  Babashka wrappers mid-card on 2026-08-30.
- Probe availability with `swarm_tool.sh require <aps-tool>` (it passes on the Lua forwarders).
  Never run `swarm_tool.sh ensure <aps-tool>`: it swaps in the Babashka wrapper and re-fetches the
  upstream Clojure clone of Acceptance-Pipeline-Specification into `.swarmforge/tools/`.
- Repair a missing or drifted forwarder (fresh clone, or after `lua tools/cli.lua distclean` run at
  the `<swarm-root>`, which is what deletes that shared `.swarmforge/`) with the project's idempotent
  provisioner, never by hand:
  `lua tools/packages/acceptance/provision.lua`. Forwarder bodies - entrypoints, `set -e`,
  mode 755, the mutator's differential clamp (`--level full` -> `--level hard`, caller `--workers`
  replaced by `--workers 4`) and the baked 5.4 interpreter - have one source of truth in
  `tools/packages/acceptance/aps_forwarders.lua`; a hand-copied `exec lua ...` lands on PATH `lua`
  (5.5 on this machine) instead of the pinned rock tree. Issue #606.
- This repo keeps no Clojure sources and no `bb` project tasks; `bb` stays installed only as the
  forge's own script runtime. `swarmforge/scripts/*.bb` are forge-overlay files: do not edit,
  do not index them as project code, do not sync this pack from the upstream GitHub swarm-forge
  (start/stop goes through the local forge dashboard).

## Verification
- Coverage: `lua tools/cli.lua verify --coverage`. luacov stats must exist and be fresh before `crap4lua`; CRAP scores without coverage stats are invalid. If coverage cannot run, hand back a blocker instead of inventing numbers.
- Acceptance suite: `lua tools/cli.lua acceptance` whenever features/ exists; Gherkin soft mutation: `lua tools/cli.lua acceptance-mutate`.
- Completion floor before every handoff: `lua tools/cli.lua verify` (slim) fully green.
- Acceptance generation and acceptance tests run sequentially; avoid running the whole-suite spec lane concurrently with acceptance generation.

## Source Conventions
- snake_case names, CamelCase classes. In src/ never use `tonumber` or `type == "number"`; use NumberUtils (`src.foundation.number`).
- Eggy `Fixed` parameters take floats (e.g. `30.0`).
- Every src file ends with an embedded mutate4lua v4 manifest. After deleting or renaming functions, regenerate it with `lua tools/cli.lua mutate <file> --update-manifest`; never hand-edit manifests.
